out.push(A('**1** _The committee **shall decide** before the tenth of January._ **2** _It is open **to** you to amend the rota._ **3** _On the information available **on** 3 May, …_ **4** _I would suggest that the registrars **ask** for two things._ _(subjunctive after_ suggest _)_ **5** _What would have to be true **for the fifth option to work**?_ **6** _The standard says inspections should be carried out, **which does not make them mandatory.**_ _(and the sentence as written joins two clauses with a comma and gets the law wrong in the same breath)_'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **Because the reader here has to act.** **In 1.7 and 3.7 the reader had nothing to write and nothing to do, so the mediation left them alone.** **A claims handler is going to decline a claim on Thursday**, so there is a fourth move: **one question to the reader, about what the reader holds.**'));
out.push(A('_(No Practise line in x.7. The Language box in a Review & Mediate cycle collects the moves and carries no Practise item — the house pattern at every level of this series.)_'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fourth mediation in four units and the first one that adds a move, so the class must be shown both halves: what has not changed, and what has.** **Unchanged: say what is correct, show the writer their own sentence, ask one question, stop.** **Added: one question to the reader, because the reader is going to act.** **Put the test on the board in those words** — ⚠ **_has this reader got something to write or something to do?_** **In 3.7 the first reader had neither, and correcting him would have been the easier of the two conversations.** **Here the lawyer is about to instruct a second engineer and the handler is about to decline a claim, and a mediator who says nothing to either of them has mediated a document rather than a dispute.** **And the finding to leave the unit on is Mr Zahreddine\'s eleven weeks: a limit is an instruction to the reader, and both readers treated the most useful sentence in the document as throat-clearing.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the lift certificate)'));
