out.push(A('⚠ **Part 2 is grammar and almost never vocabulary, which is the opposite of Part 1 and the single most useful thing to tell a class.** **Eight gaps and eight grammatical words: a relative, four prepositions or parts of fixed phrases, a connector, a conjunction and a comparative.** **Teach the mechanical first pass: read the whole text once without writing anything, then go back and for each gap name the part of speech before trying a word.** ⚠ **Items 3, 4 and 8 are fixed phrases and should be learnt as wholes** — _far from being_, _of no use_, _more often than not_ — **and item 6 is the one most candidates lose**: _so that_ **is the only two-word consecutive linker that fits, and a candidate who has not noticed the _that_ after the gap will try _meaning_ or _ensuring_ and write a word that is not grammatical.**'));
